 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return, unlimited by default. When
+the header has more ranges than this (counted after `combine`, if enabled),
+they are replaced by a single range covering from the lowest start to the
+highest end, so the result may include bytes the client did not ask for.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-1,10-11,50-51', { limit: 2 })
+// => [{ start: 0, end: 51 }]
+```
+
